      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_h_k_d_f_cache_1a148b1a9af62f36fdc32fbf90fa465825" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void themis::utils::HKDFCache::purge_by_ikm_hash</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;ikm_hash)</argsstring>
        <name>purge_by_ikm_hash</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::utils::HKDFCache::purge_by_ikm_hash</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>ikm_hash</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Purge all entries derived from a specific Input Key Material (IKM). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Purge by ikm hash.</para>
<para>Enables selective cache invalidation when a root key (IKM) is rotated. For example, after rotating a master encryption key, all keys derived from it can be invalidated via this method, forcing re-derivation with the new master key.</para>
<para>Implementation:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Scans all cache shards for entries whose IKM matches the given hash</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Securely wipes matching entries using OPENSSL_cleanse</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Updates eviction counters</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ikm_hash</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>SHA-256 hash of the IKM bytes, as hex string (lowercase) Example: &quot;abc123def456...&quot; </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Number of entries purged</para>
</simplesect>
@thread_safe Yes - internally synchronized across all shards <simplesect kind="note"><para>Performance: O(n) in worst case; consider calling during maintenance window</para>
</simplesect>
Usage Scenario: <programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Master<sp/>key<sp/>rotation<sp/>workflow</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::vector&lt;uint8_t&gt;<sp/>old_master<sp/>=<sp/>...;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::string<sp/>old_master_hash<sp/>=<sp/>sha256_hex(old_master);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cache.purge_by_ikm_hash(old_master_hash);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>New<sp/>keys<sp/>will<sp/>now<sp/>be<sp/>derived<sp/>from<sp/>new<sp/>master</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>new_key<sp/>=<sp/>cache.derive_cached(new_master,<sp/>salt,<sp/>info,<sp/>32);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1utils_1_1_h_k_d_f_cache_1a48ec353dae1b48b49f8cabb78e0c1763" kindref="member">stats()</ref> for cache efficiency monitoring</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">ikm_hash</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Calls: lk(), begin(), end(), find(), size(), <ref refid="structthemis_1_1utils_1_1_h_k_d_f_cache_1_1_impl_1ae6f56bb34878767bf0f9a97be94a7963" kindref="member">Impl::sha256_hex()</ref>, data(), std::next(). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
